  "answer_markdown": "The fine-tuning API is deprecated and no longer actively supported [1]. To steer a model to your application, Mistral recommends three methods: using a **System prompt**, **Tuning a model**, or **Deploying a moderation layer** for input/output processing [3].\n\n- **System prompt**: Provide context, instructions, and guidelines to steer model behavior, including roles, persona, tone, values, and output format [3].\n- **Tuning a model**: Train the model on your intended application behavior using approaches like application tuning or safety tuning [3]. Mistral supports tuning via open-source with the [FT Codebase](https://github.com/mistralai/mistral-finetune/) or through [AI Studio](https://console.mistral.ai/) [5].\n- **Deploy a moderation layer**: Use a classifier for content moderation as an extra security measure [3].\n\nFor tuning, you can upload and validate your training data in AI Studio, run the job, and access your custom model via your own model API endpoint [5].",
  "citations": [
    {"n": 1, "quote": "This feature is deprecated and is no longer actively supported."},
    {"n": 3, "quote": "There are several techniques (with varying levels of engineering complexity) available to steer model behavior within your application context. We recommend leveraging the three methods below to do so:"},
    {"n": 3, "quote": "A **System Prompt** is a method to provide context, instructions, and guidelines to your model before the model is tasked with user input data"},
    {"n": 3, "quote": "**Tuning a model** is a method to train the model on your intended application behavior"},
    {"n": 3, "quote": "**Deploying a classifier for content moderation** is a third method to create guardrails for your model’s behavior within the application."},
    {"n": 5, "quote": "At Mistral, we support two ways to customize our models: 1. OSS with the [FT Codebase](https://github.com/mistralai/mistral-finetune/) 2. Via the [AI Studio](https://console.mistral.ai/)"},
    {"n": 5, "quote": "Head to our FT API within the AI Studio, upload and validate your training data. Run the job, and when completed, you can access your custom model via your own model API endpoint."}
  ],
  "insufficient_evidence": false
}

