text:
{
  "answer_markdown": "Inside `json_schema` you place an object with a `schema` field that contains a valid JSON Schema (draft-07 style) describing the desired output shape, plus optional `name` and `strict` fields. For example, to require a book with a string `name` and an array of string `authors`, you would use:

```json
{
  "type": "json_schema",
  "json_schema": {
    "schema": {
      "properties": {
        "name": {
          "title": "Name",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "authors": {
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "title": "Authors",
          "type": "array"
        }
      },
      "required": ["name", "authors"],
      "title": "Book",
      "type": "object",
      "additionalProperties": false
    },
    "name": "book",
    "strict": true
  }
}
```
The `schema` must define `type`, `properties`, and `required` as needed, and `additionalProperties: false` is used to forbid extra fields [1][5].",
