{
  "answer_markdown": "Yes. The Handoffs and Agents beta features are exposed via REST endpoints such as `POST /v1/agents` and `GET /v1/agents/pages`, which you can call from any language or HTTP client [5][6]. The documentation also explicitly notes that the confirmation flow (a related capability) can be implemented via a raw REST API that works with any language or HTTP client [1].",
  "citations": [
    {
      "n": 1,
      "quote": "This works for all tool types: Connectors, built-in tools (such as `web_search_premium`), and local functions (Python SDK only). You can implement the confirmation flow in two ways: - **[REST API](https://docs.mistral.ai/studio/connectors/confirmation#raw-api)**: manage conversation IDs and tool call IDs yourself. Works with any language or HTTP client."
    },
    {
      "n": 5,
      "quote": "Create a new agent giving it instructions, tools, description. The agent is then available to be used as a regular assistant in a conversation or as part of an agent pool from which it can be used."
    },
    {
      "n": 6,
      "quote": "Retrieve a page of agent entities. Unlike the deprecated `GET /v1/agents`, this endpoint paginates by opaque cursor and honors per-agent sharing, returning only agents the caller is authorized to see."
    }
  ],
  "insufficient_evidence": false
}

