{
  "answer_markdown": "To connect from a web page, your backend must first mint a short-lived realtime token via `POST /v1/client/sessions` using your API key, then pass that token to the browser. The browser then opens the WebSocket with the token in the `Sec-WebSocket-Protocol` header, since browsers cannot set `Authorization` on WebSocket connections [1].

Backend (server-side) code to mint the token:

```bash
curl https://api.mistral.ai/v1/client/sessions \
  -X POST \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $MISTRAL_API_KEY" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "purpose": "realtime",
    "model": "voxtral-mini-transcribe-realtime-2602"
  }'
```

Browser (client-side) code to connect:

```typescript
const token = await fetchTokenFromYourBackend(); // "rt_..."
const model = "voxtral-mini-transcribe-realtime-2602";

const ws = new WebSocket(
  `wss://api.mistral.ai/v1/audio/transcriptions/realtime?model=${model}`,
  ["realtime", token] // passed as Sec-WebSocket-Protocol
);
```",
