text:
{
  "answer_markdown": "To set up the Vibe agent in a JetBrains IDE, follow these steps:\n\n1. Ensure you have **JetBrains IDE 2025.3.2 or later** and the **AI Assistant plugin** installed. If not, install the plugin via `Settings > Plugins` or by clicking `Install Plugin` in the `AI Chat` tool window [1].\n\n2. Open `Settings` (`Cmd+,` on macOS, `Ctrl+Alt+S` on Windows/Linux), then go to `Tools > AI Assistant > Agents` [1].\n\n3. Search for `Mistral Vibe` in the agent registry and click `Install` on its entry. The IDE will download the agent and required runtime [1].\n\n4. Open the `AI Chat` tool window and select `Mistral Vibe` from the agent selector at the bottom of the chat input [1].\n\n5. Authenticate with your Mistral API key when prompted. Vibe stores credentials in `~/.vibe/` and reuses them across sessions [1].\n\n6. Verify the setup by sending a test prompt, such as:\n\n```text\nExplain the currently open file.\n```\n\nVibe will use the active project and editor context [1].\n\n> **Note**: Do not use the deprecated *Mistral Code Enterprise* JetBrains plugin; the supported path is via ACP [1].\n\nVibe in JetBrains shares the same configuration (agents, skills, MCP servers) as the CLI and VS Code extension, stored in `~/.vibe/` and per-project `.vibe/` directories [1].",
  "citations": [
    {
